=== SIGNATURE ===
z_route_edges_step(costs, board, move_rule, dir_list, infinity)

=== COMMENT ===
Private worker for route_edges; do not call directly. Performs one synchronous directed-edge relaxation across the allowed directions.

=== CODE ===
=LAMBDA(costs, board, move_rule, dir_list, infinity,
  REDUCE(
    costs,
    dir_list,
    LAMBDA(best, dir,
      LET(
        prior_costs, shift_arr(costs, dir, infinity),
        from_cells, shift_arr(board, dir, ""),
        edge_costs, MAP(
          from_cells,
          board,
          LAMBDA(from_cell, to_cell, IFNA(move_rule(from_cell, to_cell, dir), infinity))
        ),
        candidates, MAP(
          prior_costs,
          edge_costs,
          LAMBDA(prior, edge,
            IF(
              NOT(ISNUMBER(edge)),
              infinity,
              IF(
                OR(edge < 0, prior >= infinity),
                infinity,
                MIN(infinity, prior + edge)
              )
            )
          )
        ),
        MAP(best, candidates, LAMBDA(current, candidate, MIN(current, candidate)))
      )
    )
  )
)

=== DESCRIPTION ===
Private one-round relaxation helper for route_edges.

For each allowed direction, shifts the prior distance grid and board so every destination cell is aligned with its predecessor. It calls move_rule(from_cell, to_cell, dir), adds each legal edge cost to the predecessor distance, and keeps the smallest candidate for every cell. All directions read the same incoming costs array, so one call advances paths by at most one edge.

Arguments:
  costs     - current least-known cost array.
  board     - map/helper array passed to move_rule.
  move_rule - LAMBDA(from_cell, to_cell, dir) returning a legal nonnegative edge cost or NA()/text/negative for an illegal edge.
  dir_list  - allowed direction arrows.
  infinity  - numeric sentinel used for unreachable cells and boundaries.

Returns:
  The improved cost array after one synchronous relaxation round.
